IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra4-s105-recovery`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 5, ss 106 to 112: deduction from earnings in other cases,
-- child benefit and guardian's allowance, the Limitation Act, fines, investigation and prosecution. Layer 1, part wra4.
-- Host Acts named in labels: SSAA (Social Security Administration Act 1992), SSA(NI)A (the Northern Ireland counterpart),
-- LA1980 (Limitation Act 1980), CJA1991 (Criminal Justice Act 1991). They are not among the sources.
-- Result convention: JUST FALSE / FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered (see wra4-ss96-97.l4).

§ `s 106 -- deduction from earnings: other cases`

-- Inserted SSAA 71(9A): regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under the provisions mentioned in 71(8) to be
-- recovered by deductions from earnings. The same shape as 71ZD(1), which this calls.
-- src:1783 | (9A) Regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under the provisions mentioned in subsection (8) above to be recovered by deductions from earnings.
@ref s 106(1) SSAA 71(9A) (src:1783-1783)
GIVEN `the amount is recoverable under a provision mentioned in SSAA section 71(8)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the amount one that is recoverable under a provision mentioned in section 71(8) of the Administration Act (overpayments in general)?
      `regulations provide for deductions from earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations provide for such amounts to be recovered by deductions from earnings? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(1) SSAA 71(9A) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` MEANS
    IF `the amount is recoverable under a provision mentioned in SSAA section 71(8)`
    THEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` `regulations provide for deductions from earnings`
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "amounts recoverable under the provisions mentioned in subsection (8)"

-- src:1784 | (9B) In subsection (9A) above “earnings” has such meaning as may be prescribed.
@ref s 106(1) SSAA 71(9B) “earnings” (src:1784-1784)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the regulations treat this payment as earnings for these deductions? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(1) SSAA 71(9B) the payment is earnings` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings`

-- Inserted SSAA 75(8): housing benefit overpayments under section 75 (the amount recoverable "under this section").
-- src:1802 | (8) Regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under this section to be recovered by deductions from earnings.
@ref s 106(3) SSAA 75(8) (src:1802-1802)
GIVEN `the amount is a housing benefit overpayment recoverable under SSAA section 75` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the amount an overpayment of housing benefit recoverable from you under section 75 of the Administration Act?
      `regulations provide for deductions from earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations provide for such amounts to be recovered by deductions from earnings? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(3) SSAA 75(8) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` MEANS
    IF `the amount is a housing benefit overpayment recoverable under SSAA section 75`
    THEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` `regulations provide for deductions from earnings`
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "amounts recoverable under this section"

-- src:1803 | (9) In subsection (8) above “earnings“ has such meaning as may be prescribed.
@ref s 106(3) SSAA 75(9) “earnings” (src:1803-1803)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the regulations treat this payment as earnings for these deductions? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(3) SSAA 75(9) the payment is earnings` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings`

-- Inserted SSAA 78(3C): amounts recoverable under 78(1) from a person specified in 78(3) (social fund awards).
-- src:1819 | (3C) Regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under subsection (1) above from a person specified in subsection (3) above to be recovered by deductions from earnings.
@ref s 106(4) SSAA 78(3C) (src:1819-1819)
GIVEN `the amount is recoverable under SSAA section 78(1) from a person specified in section 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the amount a social fund award recoverable from you under section 78 of the Administration Act?
      `regulations provide for deductions from earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations provide for such amounts to be recovered by deductions from earnings? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(4) SSAA 78(3C) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` MEANS
    IF `the amount is recoverable under SSAA section 78(1) from a person specified in section 78(3)`
    THEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` `regulations provide for deductions from earnings`
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "amounts recoverable under subsection (1) above from a person specified in subsection (3) above"

-- src:1820 | (3D) In subsection (3C) above “earnings” has such meaning as may be prescribed.
@ref s 106(4) SSAA 78(3D) “earnings” (src:1820-1820)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the regulations treat this payment as earnings for these deductions? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(4) SSAA 78(3D) the payment is earnings` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings`

-- Inserted SSAA 71ZA(2A): a reading rule. Where 71(9A) applies to social fund overpayments, its reference to amounts
-- recoverable under the provisions mentioned in 71(8) is read as a reference to amounts recoverable under 71ZA(1) and (4)
-- by virtue of 71ZA(1).
-- src:1800 | (2A) Subsection (9A) of section 71 above as it so applies shall have effect as if the reference to amounts recoverable under the provisions mentioned in subsection (8) of that section were to amounts recoverable under subsections (1) and (4) of that section by virtue of subsection (1) above.
@ref s 106(2) SSAA 71ZA(2A) (src:1800-1800)
GIVEN `the amount is recoverable under subsections (1) and (4) of SSAA section 71ZA by virtue of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the amount a social fund overpayment recoverable from you under section 71ZA(1) and (4) of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(2) SSAA 71ZA(2A) the reference in 71(9A) is read as reaching the amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount is recoverable under subsections (1) and (4) of SSAA section 71ZA by virtue of subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the reading applies to "amounts recoverable under subsections (1) and (4) of that section by virtue of subsection (1) above"

§ `s 107 -- recovery of child benefit and guardian's allowance`

-- s 107(1): the words ", other than an amount paid in respect of child benefit or guardian's allowance," are repealed from
-- SSAA 71(8) (recovery of benefits by deduction from prescribed benefits). So that exclusion no longer applies to these two.
-- src:1823 | (1) In section 71(8) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (recovery of benefits by deduction from prescribed benefits), the words “, other than an amount paid in respect of child benefit or guardian's allowance,” are repealed.
@ref s 107(1) (src:1823-1823)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) the exclusion of this benefit from SSAA 71(8) is repealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `child benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `guardian's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING                                     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the repeal removes the words about "child benefit or guardian's allowance" only

-- src:1824 | (2) In section 69(8) of the Social Security Administration (Northern Ireland) Act 1992 (recovery of benefits by deduction from prescribed benefits), the words “, other than an amount paid in respect of child benefit or guardian's allowance,” are repealed.
@ref s 107(2) (src:1824-1824)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(2) the exclusion of this benefit from SSA(NI)A 69(8) is repealed` MEANS
    `s 107(1) the exclusion of this benefit from SSAA 71(8) is repealed` `the benefit`

§ `s 108 -- application of the Limitation Act 1980`

-- Inserted LA1980 38(11): references in that Act to an action "do not include any method of recovery" of a sum recoverable under
-- Part 3 SSAA, SSCBA s 127(c) or Part 1 TCA 2002, "other than a proceeding in a court of law".
DECLARE `s 108(3) LA1980 38(11) where the sum is recoverable` IS ONE OF
    `s 108(3)(a) under Part 3 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    `s 108(3)(b) under section 127(c) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992`
    `s 108(3)(c) under Part 1 of the Tax Credits Act 2002`
    `s 108(3) under some other provision`

-- src:1830 | (11) References in this Act to an action do not include any method of recovery of a sum recoverable under—
-- src:1831 | (a) Part 3 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992,
-- src:1832 | (b) section 127(c) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, or
-- src:1833 | (c) Part 1 of the Tax Credits Act 2002,
-- src:1834 | other than a proceeding in a court of law.
@ref s 108(3) LA1980 38(11) (src:1830-1834)
GIVEN `where the sum is recoverable` IS A `s 108(3) LA1980 38(11) where the sum is recoverable`
      `the method of recovery` IS A `Way of recovering an amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(3) LA1980 38(11) the method of recovery is an “action” for the Limitation Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the sum is recoverable`
    WHEN `s 108(3) under some other provision` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the exclusion covers the three Acts named
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the method of recovery`
        WHEN `court action` THEN NOTHING                  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "other than a proceeding in a court of law"; whether it is an action is for the Limitation Act itself
        WHEN `deduction from benefit` THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Act to an action do not include any method of recovery of a sum recoverable under"
        WHEN `deduction from earnings` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Act to an action do not include any method of recovery of a sum recoverable under"
        WHEN `adjustment of benefit` THEN JUST FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Act to an action do not include any method of recovery of a sum recoverable under"

-- s 108(4): the amendments have effect as if in force when s 38 of the 1980 Act was, "except for the purposes of proceedings
-- brought before the coming into force of this section".
-- src:1835 | (4) The amendments made by this section have effect as if they had come into force at the same time as section 38 of the Limitation Act 1980, except for the purposes of proceedings brought before the coming into force of this section.
@ref s 108(4) (src:1835-1835)
GIVEN `the proceedings were brought before this section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Were the proceedings brought before section 108 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(4) the amendments apply to the proceedings as if in force from the start` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were brought before this section came into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purposes of proceedings brought before the coming into force of this section"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `s 109 -- recovery of fines by deduction from employment and support allowance`

-- s 109(1)(a): "income-related" is repealed in CJA1991 s 24(1) and (2)(d), so the limit to income-related employment and
-- support allowance is gone. s 109(3): the repeals have effect as if in force on 27 October 2008.
-- src:1839 | (a) in subsections (1) and (2)(d) the words “income-related” are repealed;
-- src:1842 | (3) The repeals made by this section have effect as if they had come into force on 27 October 2008.
@ref s 109(1)(a) and (3) (src:1839-1842)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109 CJA1991 s 24 “income-related” no longer limits the allowance on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN
        IF `the day` AT LEAST (Date 27 10 2008) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the repeal has effect from 27 October 2008; the text does not say what the position was before
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN
        IF `the day` AT LEAST (Date 27 10 2008) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the repeal has effect from 27 October 2008; the text does not say what the position was before
    OTHERWISE NOTHING                                     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the repeal concerns employment and support allowance only

§ `s 110 -- powers to require information relating to investigations`

-- Inserted SSAA 109B(2)(ia): a person "of a prescribed description" is added to those who may be required to supply information.
-- src:1847 | (ia) a person of a prescribed description;
@ref s 110(a) SSAA 109B(2)(ia) (src:1847-1847)
GIVEN `the person is of a description regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Are you of a description that the regulations prescribe as one who may be required to give information for an investigation? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(a) SSAA 109B(2)(ia) the person may be required to supply information for an investigation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is of a description regulations prescribe`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                          -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (ia) adds one class to a list the host section keeps open; the text does not say anyone else is exempt
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a person of a prescribed description"

§ `s 112 -- prosecution powers of local authorities (SSAA 116ZA)`

DECLARE `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) subject of a direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a particular authority`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a description of authority`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) particular proceedings`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a description of proceedings`

DECLARE `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(a) whether the proceedings should be instituted`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(b) what charges should be preferred`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(c) what representations to make to a magistrates' court about mode of trial`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(d) whether to discontinue proceedings`
    `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7) any other decision`

-- 116ZA(2) with (1), (3), (5) and (9): the authority "may not bring proceedings ... unless" one of (a) to (e); the Secretary
-- of State may direct that it may not bring them under (a), (b) or (c) despite their being met; conditions prescribed under
-- (5) must be satisfied ("only if"); the section "does not apply to Scotland".
-- src:1857 | (1) This section applies to an authority administering housing benefit or council tax benefit.
-- src:1858 | (2) The authority may not bring proceedings against a person for a benefit offence relating to either of those benefits unless—
-- src:1859 | (a) the authority has already started an investigation in relation to that person in respect of the offence,
-- src:1860 | (b) in a case where the proceedings relate to housing benefit, the authority has already started an investigation in relation to the person in respect of a benefit offence relating to council tax benefit, or has already brought proceedings against the person in respect of such an offence,
-- src:1861 | (c) in a case where the proceedings relate to council tax benefit, the authority has already started an investigation in relation to the person in respect of a benefit offence relating to housing benefit, or has already brought proceedings against the person in respect of such an offence,
-- src:1862 | (d) the proceedings arise in prescribed circumstances or are of a prescribed description, or
-- src:1863 | (e) the Secretary of State has directed that the authority may bring the proceedings.
-- src:1864 | (3) The Secretary of State may direct that in prescribed circumstances, an authority may not bring proceedings by virtue of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c) despite the requirements in those provisions being met.
-- src:1865 | (4) A direction under subsection (2)(e) or (3) may relate to a particular authority or description of authority or to particular proceedings or any description of proceedings.
-- src:1866 | (5) If the Secretary of State prescribes conditions for the purposes of this section, an authority may bring proceedings in accordance with this section only if any such condition is satisfied.
-- src:1878 | (9) This section does not apply to Scotland.
@ref s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(1), (2), (3), (5) and (9) (src:1857-1878)
GIVEN `where the proceedings would be brought` IS A Place  @desc Where would the proceedings be brought?
      `the authority administers housing benefit or council tax benefit` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the authority bringing the proceedings administer housing benefit or council tax benefit?
      `the authority has already started an investigation of this offence` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the authority already started an investigation into this offence?
      `the proceedings relate to housing benefit and the authority has already investigated or prosecuted a council tax benefit offence by the person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc If the proceedings are about housing benefit: has the authority already started an investigation, or brought proceedings, about a council tax benefit offence by you?
      `the proceedings relate to council tax benefit and the authority has already investigated or prosecuted a housing benefit offence by the person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc If the proceedings are about council tax benefit: has the authority already started an investigation, or brought proceedings, about a housing benefit offence by you?
      `a direction under subsection (3) says the authority may not bring them despite (a), (b) or (c) being met` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that the authority may not bring these proceedings even though it had already started an investigation?
      `the proceedings arise in prescribed circumstances or are of a prescribed description` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the proceedings arise in circumstances, or are they of a description, that the regulations prescribe? Leave out if not known.
      `the Secretary of State has directed that the authority may bring the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that the authority may bring these proceedings?
      `a condition prescribed under subsection (5) is not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the Secretary of State prescribed a condition for bringing these proceedings that is not satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(2) the authority may bring proceedings for the benefit offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `where the proceedings would be brought` EQUALS Scotland
        THEN JUST FALSE                                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(9) This section does not apply to Scotland"
        IF (NOT (`the authority administers housing benefit or council tax benefit`))
        THEN NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "This section applies to an authority administering housing benefit or council tax benefit"
        IF `a condition prescribed under subsection (5) is not satisfied`
        THEN JUST FALSE                                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an authority may bring proceedings in accordance with this section only if any such condition is satisfied"
        IF (`the authority has already started an investigation of this offence`
              OR `the proceedings relate to housing benefit and the authority has already investigated or prosecuted a council tax benefit offence by the person`
              OR `the proceedings relate to council tax benefit and the authority has already investigated or prosecuted a housing benefit offence by the person`)
           AND (NOT (`a direction under subsection (3) says the authority may not bring them despite (a), (b) or (c) being met`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Secretary of State has directed that the authority may bring the proceedings`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE (CONSIDER `the proceedings arise in prescribed circumstances or are of a prescribed description`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authority may not bring proceedings against a person for a benefit offence ... unless" one of (a) to (e)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed circumstances" are for regulations

-- 116ZA(4): a direction under (2)(e) or (3) may relate to any of four things.
-- src:1865 | (4) A direction under subsection (2)(e) or (3) may relate to a particular authority or description of authority or to particular proceedings or any description of proceedings.
@ref s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(4) (src:1865-1865)
GIVEN `the subject` IS A `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) subject of a direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(4) a direction may relate to the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a particular authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a description of authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) particular proceedings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(4) a description of proceedings` THEN TRUE

-- 116ZA(6): the Secretary of State may continue the proceedings as if brought in his name, or discontinue them, "if" (a) they
-- were brought under (2)(a), (b) or (c), (b) provision under (2)(d) means the authority could no longer bring them, (c) he
-- withdraws a direction under (2)(e), or (d) a condition prescribed under (5) ceases to be satisfied.
-- src:1867 | (6) The Secretary of State may continue proceedings which have been brought by an authority in accordance with this section as if the proceedings had been brought in his name or he may discontinue the proceedings if—
-- src:1868 | (a) the proceedings were brought by virtue of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c),
-- src:1869 | (b) he makes provision under subsection (2)(d) which has the effect that the authority would no longer be entitled to bring the proceedings in accordance with this section,
-- src:1870 | (c) he withdraws a direction under subsection (2)(e) in relation to the proceedings, or
-- src:1871 | (d) a condition prescribed under subsection (5) ceases to be satisfied in relation to the proceedings.
@ref s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(6) (src:1867-1871)
GIVEN `the proceedings were brought by virtue of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Were the proceedings brought because the authority had already started an investigation?
      `provision under subsection (2)(d) means the authority would no longer be entitled to bring them` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has new regulation-made provision taken away the authority's entitlement to bring these proceedings?
      `the Secretary of State withdraws the direction under subsection (2)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the Secretary of State withdrawn the direction that allowed the authority to bring these proceedings?
      `a condition prescribed under subsection (5) ceases to be satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has a condition prescribed for bringing these proceedings ceased to be satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(6) the Secretary of State may continue or discontinue the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were brought by virtue of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c)`
       OR `provision under subsection (2)(d) means the authority would no longer be entitled to bring them`
       OR `the Secretary of State withdraws the direction under subsection (2)(e)`
       OR `a condition prescribed under subsection (5) ceases to be satisfied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may continue proceedings ... or he may discontinue the proceedings if" (a), (b), (c) or (d); none holds (a failed "if")

-- 116ZA(7): in exercising the power, a local authority "must have regard to the Code for Crown Prosecutors" in four decisions.
-- src:1872 | (7) In exercising a power to bring proceedings in accordance with this section, a local authority must have regard to the Code for Crown Prosecutors issued by the Director of Public Prosecutions under section 10 of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985—
-- src:1873 | (a) in determining whether the proceedings should be instituted;
-- src:1874 | (b) in determining what charges should be preferred;
-- src:1875 | (c) in considering what representations to make to a magistrates'court about mode of trial;
-- src:1876 | (d) in determining whether to discontinue proceedings.
@ref s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(7) (src:1872-1876)
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7) decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) SSAA 116ZA(7) the local authority must have regard to the Code for Crown Prosecutors in the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(a) whether the proceedings should be instituted` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(b) what charges should be preferred` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(c) what representations to make to a magistrates' court about mode of trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7)(d) whether to discontinue proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 112 SSAA 116ZA(7) any other decision` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the duty is stated "(a)" to "(d)" and for no other decision
